<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Templated from VFEP's VFEP_WarcasketShoulders_Cataphract (VFEP v3.09, commit 31cee5e,
    1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/Apparel_Various.xml); fields not discussed here are the
    Cataphract's. Tier, research, tags, plating, weight and the art follow the armor's header.

    - ToxicEnvironmentResistance +0.15, the shoulders' share of the set's 1.2 (rationale in the
      armor's header).
    - Costs: Comp 2 is the gas jet's nozzle (VFEP's Controller shoulders likewise pay components
      for their verb); Steel 55 and Plasteel 20 put the piece in the 7th-gen band. Chemfuel 15
      pays part of the nozzle's own two jets, which come filled (40), on the armor's middle
      ground between VFEP's free fill and vanilla's up-front one.

    Gas jet: an apparel verb (ToxinWarcasket.Verb_SprayGas), as the Barrage shoulders carry
    theirs, so this piece redeclares tickerType Normal for the verb tracker and the AI check (the
    shoulder base leaves it at Never). A jet is two thirds of a tox pack, shaped: 10 tank charges
    at the armor's 3 cells each are 30 cells against the pack's 45, spread evenly over the cells
    the cone reaches. A 12 degree half-angle cone from 3 cells out to 12.9 is about 32 cells, so
    an open cone lands just under full density; walls shrink the cone and concentrate it, and
    past a full cell GasGrid.AddGas thickens the edges with the excess. coneStart 3: the angle
    test makes the cone a single-cell line for its first four cells, the pilot is immune and
    whoever stands beside them is not, and a one-wide stem bleeds sideways as much as any edge,
    so the shot begins where the cone is already three wide. The gas then spreads past the cone
    as the grid equalizes neighbours down to a step of 34, so the targeter draws two areas: the
    cone the gas lands in, and around it the cells expected to hold spreadMinGas or more within
    spreadTicks of the shot, from GasSpreadEstimate's replay of the grid's own rules. The
    threshold is 1, any gas at all, because that is what the player sees: SectionLayer_Gas hands
    each cell's raw density to the vertex colour, which clamps to 1, so a cell holding one unit
    draws exactly like a full one and the cloud shows no dose. The outer area is therefore where
    the cloud will show, and the cone itself is the part that bites: the first ring gets half the
    cone's density on the grid's first push, the next a quarter, the third a trace. At the
    defaults that is about 133 cells, four times the cone, three rings deep and back to the
    pilot's neighbours, which is the cloud a shot leaves on open ground. halfAngle, range and
    the 1 s warmupTime are the defaults of their mod settings.
    - Fuel (ToxinWarcasket.CompJetNozzle): 20 charges from the armor's tank, and nothing else
      while one is worn; with the tank short the command is disabled with the tank's shortfall.
      Worn without a tank, the nozzle's own two jets are the fuel, each reloaded with those
      charges' 20 chemfuel, so the shoulders stay useful alone; they are a fallback, not a
      supply on top of the tank's, so a worn tank leaves them unspent and unreloaded
      (Patches/CompApparelReloadable_Reload). tankChargesPerShot and maxCharges are the defaults
      of their mod settings (the jet's cost and jets without a tank), and the settings recompute
      ammoCountPerCharge as the cost times the armor's chemfuel per charge, so the 20 here is
      only the default's product. The command's corner counts the jets the worn supply holds: a
      full tank reads 4 / 4, the shoulders alone 2 / 2. Its label is jetLabel, which the comp
      writes onto the verb because the translation walker never reaches a WarcasketDef's verbs,
      and its tooltip is jetDescription, as the gear's own description is the set's lore.
    - onlyManualCast, as the Barrage's: a drafted colonist never fires it on its own. Raiders
      fire it through the nozzle's own check, at the densest group of hostile humanlikes the gas
      would affect, never into their own faction's.

    Compat: SOS2Patch.xml leaves shoulder pads alone, as VFEP's own patch does for VFEP's.
  -->
  <VFEPirates.WarcasketDef ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketShoulderPadBase">
    <defName>TXWC_WarcasketShoulders_Toxin</defName>
    <label>toxin warcasket shoulders</label>
    <shortDescription>Specialized warcasket pauldrons with superior protection and worse weight, fitted with shoulder-mounted jets that spray tox gas from the shell's tank.</shortDescription>
    <description>Specialized warcasket pauldrons with superior protection and worse weight, fitted with shoulder-mounted jets that spray tox gas from the shell's tank.\n\nThe 7th generation warcaskets came after underwhelming results in improving the baseline performance even further, instead focusing on creating designs that - while interchangeable - work better as a set. They were also the first to include plasteel in the design as it appeared more frequently in scavenging and looting. Each piece has a unique function that synergises with those of the same series, making them a truly separate class of mobile armor units.\n\nThe Toxin series is based on the Cataphract design, rebuilt for chemical warfare. A tank in the shell feeds vents around the pilot and gas jets on the pauldrons, and the helmet's respirator draws gas back into the tank. Together the pieces make the pilot immune to environmental toxins.</description>
    <tickerType>Normal</tickerType>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketToxin/WarcasketToxinShoulders</texPath>
      <shaderType>CutoutComplex</shaderType>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>30</Mass>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>1.65</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>0.72</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>0.86</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Insulation_Cold>18</Insulation_Cold>
      <Insulation_Heat>6</Insulation_Heat>
      <EquipDelay>1</EquipDelay>
    </statBases>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <MoveSpeed>-0.30</MoveSpeed>
      <ToxicEnvironmentResistance>0.15</ToxicEnvironmentResistance>
      <SlaveSuppressionOffset MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">0.2</SlaveSuppressionOffset>
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <costList>
      <ComponentIndustrial>2</ComponentIndustrial>
      <Steel>55</Steel>
      <Plasteel>20</Plasteel>
      <Chemfuel>15</Chemfuel>
    </costList>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>VFEP_SpecialisedWarcaskets</li>
      <li>ToxGas</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <apparel>
      <bodyPartGroups>
        <li>Shoulders</li>
        <li>Arms</li>
        <li>Hands</li>
        <li>Neck</li>
      </bodyPartGroups>
      <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketToxin/WarcasketToxinShoulders</wornGraphicPath>
      <useWornGraphicMask>true</useWornGraphicMask>
      <layers>
        <li>OnSkin</li>
        <li>Middle</li>
        <li>Shell</li>
      </layers>
      <tags>
        <li>WarcasketSpecialised</li>
        <li>WarcasketAll</li>
      </tags>
    </apparel>
    <comps>
      <li Class="ToxinWarcasket.CompProperties_JetNozzle">
        <maxCharges>2</maxCharges>
        <chargeNoun>jet</chargeNoun>
        <ammoDef>Chemfuel</ammoDef>
        <ammoCountPerCharge>20</ammoCountPerCharge>
        <baseReloadTicks>60</baseReloadTicks>
        <soundReload>Standard_Reload</soundReload>
        <hotKey>Misc4</hotKey>
        <displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>false</displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>
        <tankChargesPerShot>20</tankChargesPerShot>
        <jetLabel>spray gas</jetLabel>
        <jetDescription>Spray a cone of tox gas from the shoulders toward the target. The gas lands in the inner cone and drifts over the outer area, thinning as it goes. Each jet draws on the warcasket's tank. Without a tank, the shoulders fall back on jets of their own, reloaded with chemfuel.</jetDescription>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <verbs>
      <li Class="ToxinWarcasket.VerbProperties_SprayGas">
        <hasStandardCommand>true</hasStandardCommand>
        <onlyManualCast>true</onlyManualCast>
        <range>12.9</range>
        <warmupTime>1</warmupTime>
        <noiseRadius>4</noiseRadius>
        <commandIcon>UI/Abilities/WarcasketToxin/GasJet</commandIcon>
        <soundCast>GasPack_Deploy</soundCast>
        <targetParams>
          <canTargetLocations>true</canTargetLocations>
        </targetParams>
        <halfAngle>12</halfAngle>
        <coneStart>3</coneStart>
        <propagationSpeed>0.6</propagationSpeed>
        <spreadMinGas>1</spreadMinGas>
        <spreadTicks>300</spreadTicks>
        <sprayEffecter>TXWC_GasJetSpray</sprayEffecter>
        <sprayEffecterTicks>14</sprayEffecterTicks>
      </li>
    </verbs>
  </VFEPirates.WarcasketDef>
</Defs>
